"settings.midi" = "MIDI";
"settings.midi.bend" = "Send pitch bend";
"settings.midi.bendHint" = "Off: every note keeps its nearest semitone and no bend is sent. On: the chips' fine pitch (detune, vibrato, slides) reaches the instrument as bend.";
"settings.midi.explanation" = "Bends mean nothing without the receiving instrument's range, and MIDI never reports it: say what this instrument uses.";
"settings.midi.range" = "Pitch bend range";
"settings.midi.rangeHint" = "Semitones each way. It has to match the receiving instrument: a 50 cent bend encoded for +/- 2 semitones plays as 3 semitones on a +/- 12 one. The range is declared with RPN 0 when playback starts, so a synth that honours RPN follows this value.";
"settings.midi.semitones" = "st";
"settings.midi.sampleRoot" = "Transpose by the sample's root";
"settings.midi.sampleRootHint" = "Off (default): a sampled voice is placed by the transposition the registers ask for - 1200 x log2(playback rate / the chip's reference rate) - so every interval inside one sample is exact and the absolute octave follows a documented constant. On: the root measured out of the sample's own bytes is added, which puts the octave right but can be wrong by a constant (the measurement is an inference). A voice whose root cannot be measured, or that has no pitch at all, stays a one-shot C4 trigger either way. Switching reloads the current song and keeps its position.";
"settings.midi.sampleRootRecommended" = "Recommended for PCM-based chips - Capcom QSound, C140, C352, K053260, K054539, SegaPCM, GA20, RF5C164, ES5503, OKIM6295. FM and PSG voices are unaffected. Switching reloads the current song and keeps the position.";

